{
  "name": "default",
  "description": "Default style scheme, inversion-aware for Obsidian. Obsidian core app.css applies `filter: invert(100%) hue-rotate(180deg) saturate(1.25)` to `.theme-dark .mermaid > svg` — dark mode only, whole-SVG raster filter after render; light mode renders source hex literally. Source colours are authored so both modes read: dark plate + #fff text in light mode → light plate + black text in dark mode (invert flips both). Per-kind init blocks carry the whole `%%{init: ...}%%` line — drawer agents emit them verbatim. mermaid 11.13 mechanism notes: flow/nav/architecture/tree/state/decision-tree colour via classDef in the fence body (flowchart honours it); block-beta (layout/screen-scheme/controls-scheme) via `themeCSS` role selectors `.node.<role> rect` + `.cluster.composite` because classDef never reaches block nodes; erd via `rowOdd`/`rowEven` (attributeBackgroundColorOdd/Even dead since the 11.5 unified renderer) plus a `themeCSS` white edge-label plate with black text; journey via `textPlacement:'old'` (forces SVG <text> so it inverts, instead of the default foreignObject <div> which does not) + `themeCSS` `rect.section-type-N`/`rect.task-type-N` fills. mermaid's directive sanitizer drops array-typed init keys (journey sectionFills/sectionColours/actorColours) — themeCSS is the only reliable channel.",
